   "name": "can_register_band_quantization",
   "definition": "A resident's register affinity toward a discrete relationship band is a saturating function of that band's accumulated closeness, quantized onto a resolution_bins-sized grid (the SAME trait and composition formula CAN belief quantization already uses) and classified against a small held label codebook via Argmin nearest-point decode -- the register-domain sibling of can_native_basin_decode's belief-domain basin classification, sized for a scalar classification problem rather than a relational one.",
   "why": "The mechanism BIGVILLE_TOPIC_AND_STYLE_SCOPING.md's Part 3.4 named as OCELOT's own job, not Bigville's -- a personality-trait-quantized codebook applied per discrete relationship band, reusing resolution_bins rather than inventing a second resolution trait."
  }
 ],
